# v0.225.9 Release Notes

File: openOODA/audit/release_notes/RELEASE_NOTES_v0.225.9.oot

Release: v0.225.9
Date: 2026-08-26
Tag: v0.225.9
Lane: AArch64 backend (Sovereign Native Compiler)
Worker: Mavis

## Product Path

AArch64 source-only release. No CLI surface change. The next clean
`oodac` rebuild will surface these changes; until then, the in-tree
binary at 19:32 (LLVM lane + this AArch64 lane) is the build under
verification. The 8-gate enforcer is green (byte-identical double-run).

## AArch64 Lane: AAPCS64 V0-V31 NEON Register Conventions

1. **`ooda/std/hw/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo`** — grew from 97 to 162 lines.
   Added eight public functions for the NEON/FP register file:
   `abi_fp_arg_count`, `abi_fp_arg_reg`, `abi_fp_ret_reg`, `abi_fp_ret_hi_reg`,
   `abi_is_fp_arg_reg`, `abi_is_fp_callee_saved`, `abi_valid_fp_reg`,
   `abi_fp_indirect_result_reg`.

   AAPCS64 rules now fully named for both register files:
   - **Integer file** (existing): X0-X7 args, X19-X28 callee-saved,
     X29 FP, X30 LR, X31 SP, 16-byte stack alignment.
   - **NEON/FP file** (new): V0-V7 args + scratch (caller-saved),
     V8 indirect result (caller-saved), V8-V15 lower NEON (caller-saved),
     V16-V31 upper NEON (callee-saved).

   The 4-element Academy header is updated to 6 beats, all in
   ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English.

## AArch64 Lane: Two Lock Smokes for the NEON Conventions

2. **`ooda/scripts/aarch64_neon_abi_smoke.oo`** (64 lines, 27 assertions) —
   runtime smoke that directly imports `aarch64_abi.oo` and asserts the
   values of every NEON helper. Typechecks OK. Runtime execution is
   blocked by a pre-existing `OoRes_S` / `OoRes_I` C-side type collision
   in the chs_rt runtime header that affects every `aarch64_*_smoke.oo`
   on the current host; not introduced by this smoke.

3. **`ooda/scripts/aarch64_neon_abi_source_smoke.oo`** (55 lines) —
   source-lock smoke that uses grep + subprocess instead of importing
   the ABI module. Locks the eight helpers, the AAPCS64 comment block,
   and the `aarch64_abi.oo <= 256` line cap. Manual grep verification
   on the current tree:

       grep -c "abi_fp_\|abi_is_fp_\|abi_valid_fp" std/hw/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo
       9
       grep -q "V0-V7"   std/hw/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo && echo OK  -> OK
       grep -q "V8-V15"  std/hw/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo && echo OK  -> OK
       grep -q "V16-V31" std/hw/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo && echo OK  -> OK
       grep -q "callee-saved" std/hw/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo && echo OK -> OK
       grep -q "caller-saved" std/hw/arch_aarch64/aarch64_abi.oo && echo OK -> OK

## AArch64 Lane: Type-Annotation Repairs

4. **`oodac/aarch64_emit_alu.oo`** (commit 95c39311) — added 14 type
   annotations to satisfy QUICKREF §1.4 mandatory type-annotation law.
   Restored the missing `import "aarch64_emit_int.oo";` so
   `aarch64_emit_int_write` resolves. File grew 205 to 206 lines (cap 256).

5. **`oodac/aarch64_emit_secret.oo`** (commit 95c39311) — added 19 type
   annotations to satisfy the same law. File stayed at 202 lines.

After commit 95c39311, the full GAS-text dispatch chain
(`aarch64_main.oo` -> `aarch64_emit.oo` -> all 23 arms) typechecks OK.
The in-flight background `oodac_pure_build` second stage reverts
these annotations on each cycle; the AST-path entry driver
(`aarch64_ast_main.oo` at commit 0788bce2) is the robust alternative
when the build reverts again. The typecheck lock smoke
(`aarch64_dispatch_typecheck_smoke.oo` at commit 32b4e3d1) catches any
regression.

## Audit and Documentation

6. **`openOODA/audit/aarch64-neon-abi-and-enforcer.oot`** (211 lines) —
   records the AAPCS64 changes, the type-annotation repairs, the
   enforcer 8-gate pass, the line counts, the next-step queue, the
   two lock smokes, the AST-vs-GAS-text typecheck split, and the
   manual source-smoke verification transcript.

## Verification

- 8-gate enforcer (`openOODA/scripts/enforcer.oo`) — green,
  byte-identical across two consecutive runs.
- 5 AArch64 AST codegen modules typecheck OK:
  `aarch64_abi.oo`, `aarch64_codegen.oo`, `aarch64_lower.oo`,
  `aarch64_linker.oo`, `aarch64_encoder.oo`.
- `aarch64_emit_elf.oo`, `aarch64_emit_str.oo`, `aarch64_emit_match.oo`
  typecheck OK.
- Full GAS-text dispatch chain typechecks OK (after 95c39311):
  `aarch64_main.oo` -> `aarch64_emit.oo` -> 23 arms.
- AST-path entry driver `aarch64_ast_main.oo` typechecks OK.
- 5 source-lock smokes committed:
  `aarch64_neon_abi_smoke.oo`, `aarch64_neon_abi_source_smoke.oo`,
  `aarch64_ast_entry_smoke.oo`, `aarch64_ast_pipeline_smoke.oo`,
  `aarch64_dispatch_typecheck_smoke.oo`.
- End-to-end cross-assemble proof (host machine):
  `oodac/oodac.aarch64 emit-aarch64 fixtures/aarch64_hello.oo > hello.s`
  -> `clang -target aarch64-linux-gnu -c hello.s -o hello.o` produces
  a valid ARM aarch64 ELF64 object.

## Residual

- Tier 0 closure (ROADMAP.oot §5.2): List[T] port, no_output detector,
  5-shape refuse gate.
- Tier 1 wiring: deprecate the hand-written GAS path in
  `aarch64_emit_sys.oo:60` and call `aarch64_compile_to_elf` from
  `aarch64_emit_elf.oo` directly.
- Tier 2 probe: `qemu-aarch64 -L /usr/aarch64-linux-gnu` run on each
  of the 53 aarch64 fixtures.
- Host environment: repair the `OoRes_S` / `OoRes_I` chs_rt header
  collision so all `aarch64_*_smoke.oo` can run.
